{
  "id": "RLSA-2026:95370",
  "title": "Important: kernel security update",
  "issued": {
    "date": "2026-11-06 12:04:35"
  },
  "updated": {
    "date": "2026-11-10 00:14:41"
  },
  "severity": "Important",
  "description": "The kernel packages contain the Linux kernel, the core of any Linux operating system.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* kernel: net/smc: fix UAF in smc_cdc_rx_handler() by pinning the socket (CVE-2026-64541)\n\n* kernel: sctp: avoid auth_enable sysctl UAF during netns teardown (CVE-2026-68162)\n\n* kernel: s390/zcrypt: Validate length for CCA AES cipher key requests (CVE-2026-68452)\n\n* kernel: s390/zcrypt: Validate length for CCA ECC private key requests (CVE-2026-68451)\n\n* kernel: sunrpc: pin svc_xprt across the asynchronous TLS handshake callback (CVE-2026-72222)\n\n* kernel: sunrpc: wait for in-flight TLS handshake callback when cancel loses race (CVE-2026-72221)\n\n* kernel: fs/resctrl: Fix use-after-free during unmount (CVE-2026-72080)\n\n* kernel: sctp: keep chunk-\u003etransport in step with the list it is queued on (CVE-2026-74588)\n\n* kernel: sctp: clear new_transport when removing a peer (CVE-2026-74586)\n\n* kernel: sctp: validate cookie AUTH state before use (CVE-2026-74752)\n\n* kernel: s390/vfio_ccw: Cancel existing workqueues (CVE-2026-80553)\n\n* kernel: powerpc/pseries: papr-phy-attest - validate cmd.length, plug mem leak (CVE-2026-80571)\n\n* kernel: s390/qeth: validate user buffer length in SNMP and ARP query ioctls (CVE-2026-80584)\n\n* kernel: sctp: stop processing a packet once its association is deleted (CVE-2026-89479)\n\n* kernel: openvswitch: Fix CT limit teardown use-after-free (CVE-2026-89488)\n\n* kernel: s390/boot: Avoid IPL parameter append past command line (CVE-2026-98403)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.",
